{
  "slug": "session-normalizer",
  "name": "Session Normalizer",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Auto-cleanup junk sessions on startup, show project-relevant sessions as context, and merge old sessions into project docs. Sessions carry accumulated knowledge about your\nproject — decisions made, bugs fixed, architecture chosen. This plugin consolidates that knowledge so it's never lost when sessions pile up, and surfaces the right session\nwhen you return to a project.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **4 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `session-manager` (Use when session initialization context shows \"SESSION NORMALIZER\" with recent sessions listed, or when the user asks about…)\n- **Commands** (4): `compose-brief` (Emit a project memory brief from ~/.claude/project-sessions/<slug>/history.jsonl with continuation framing), `normalize-sessions` (Project-grouped, resume-first session normalization (v2.1)), `resume-smart` (Re-trigger the session-manager resume flow mid-session), `switch-project` (Switch to a different project mid-session)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install session-normalizer@claude-community` from `mutale/session-normalizer`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 4
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
